For the castle and Ludios, if I'm interested in looting the soldiers
(rather than a) smashing with drawbridge or leaving them sleeping, or
b) simply not going there, respectively) I'd rather use a cockatrice
corpse.  Just stand off of an orthogal or diagonal and when they're
all statues zap them with a wand of striking.  This way you get to
collect almost all of their scrolls (except maybe create monster?),
potions (except acid or gain level), and wands.  Sure a cockatrice
corpse can be dangerous but they're also faster, easier on the
interface, and don't require skill slot dedication.

The only time I've consistently used a polearm was when I was jousting
with a knight and it was actually pretty fun to be able to hit
monsters at a distance and then joust them when they stepped next to
me.

